{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c7f2a9d1-4b6e-4f0a-8c3d-assessment-module",
    "name": "IRP - Assessment Module",
    "description": "Generate → start → submit flow for candidate skill assessments. Difficulty is resolved server-side from the candidate's latest resume (yearsOfExperience): <2 EASY, 2-5 MEDIUM, >5 HARD, no resume on file defaults to EASY.\n\nAll requests require a bearer token (candidateId is taken from the JWT principal, never from the request body).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      { "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Generate Assessment",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jobId\": \"{{jobId}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/assessments/generate",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["assessments", "generate"]
        },
        "description": "candidateId comes from the JWT (AuthenticationPrincipal), only jobId is in the body. Difficulty is resolved from the candidate's most recent resume's yearsOfExperience.\n\nWill throw a cooldown error (check GLOBAL_EXCEPTION_HANDLER_ADDITIONS mapping) if this candidate already generated an assessment for this job within the configured cooldown window (default 30 days).\n\nRun the resume upload request first if you want to test a specific difficulty tier."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test('Response has assessmentId and questions', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.assessmentId).to.exist;",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.questions).to.be.an('array');",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (jsonData.assessmentId) {",
              "    pm.environment.set('assessmentId', jsonData.assessmentId);",
              "}",
              "",
              "if (jsonData.questions && jsonData.questions.length > 0) {",
              "    pm.environment.set('questionId1', jsonData.questions[0].id);",
              "    if (jsonData.questions.length > 1) {",
              "        pm.environment.set('questionId2', jsonData.questions[1].id);",
              "    }",
              "}",
              "",
              "pm.test('difficultyLevel is one of EASY/MEDIUM/HARD', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(['EASY', 'MEDIUM', 'HARD']).to.include(jsonData.difficultyLevel);",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Start Assessment",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/assessments/{{assessmentId}}/start",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["assessments", "{{assessmentId}}", "start"]
        },
        "description": "Flips status GENERATED -> IN_PROGRESS and opens the start window (default 48h) within which the candidate must submit."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('status is IN_PROGRESS', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('IN_PROGRESS');",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Get Assessment",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/assessments/{{assessmentId}}",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["assessments", "{{assessmentId}}"]
        },
        "description": "Fetch current assessment state — useful to re-check questions/status without generating a new attempt."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Submit Assessment",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"assessmentId\": \"{{assessmentId}}\",\n  \"answers\": [\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"{{questionId1}}\",\n      \"selectedOption\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"{{questionId2}}\",\n      \"selectedOption\": \"B\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tabSwitchCount\": 0\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/assessments/submit",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["assessments", "submit"]
        },
        "description": "selectedOption must be one of A/B/C/D (validated by @Pattern). This sample body only fills in 2 of the 20 questions the real assessment generates — add the remaining questionId/selectedOption pairs from the 'Generate Assessment' response before running a full test, or extend the answers array manually.\n\ntabSwitchCount is reported by the frontend anti-cheat tracker; values >= the configured threshold (default 3) flag the attempt as flaggedForCheating in the result."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test('Result has score and status COMPLETED', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.score).to.be.a('number');",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.status).to.eql('COMPLETED');",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('flaggedForCheating matches tabSwitchCount logic', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.flaggedForCheating).to.be.a('boolean');",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Negative: Submit with invalid selectedOption",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"assessmentId\": \"{{assessmentId}}\",\n  \"answers\": [\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"{{questionId1}}\",\n      \"selectedOption\": \"Z\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tabSwitchCount\": 0\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/assessments/submit",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["assessments", "submit"]
        },
        "description": "selectedOption 'Z' fails the @Pattern(^[ABCD]$) validation on SubmitAnswerDTO. Expect a 400 with a validation error body (shape depends on your GlobalExceptionHandler)."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 400 Bad Request', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Negative: Generate during cooldown",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jobId\": \"{{jobId}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/assessments/generate",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["assessments", "generate"]
        },
        "description": "Re-run request #1 (same candidate + jobId) immediately after a successful generate. Expect a CooldownActiveException to be thrown and mapped to an error response — check the status code your GlobalExceptionHandler assigns it in GLOBAL_EXCEPTION_HANDLER_ADDITIONS.java."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Cooldown blocks regeneration (not 200)', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.not.eql(200);",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "response": []
    }
  ]
}